Z||000023||DaRkLoRD||12-31-2000||03:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>if jack just keeps his idea posted in his website, we can all just print it ourselves at home, any color or size we want on 'decal' paper from our printer. it sticks on the inside of your glass. with cliffs approval of course. That way wed all have same logo, but very individualized.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm sure my printer could do a fairly decent job of that, but I'd rather spend the $5 or so and get a professionally printed one.. The first run of Fieroproject cards were done on my own computer, and to be honest, they were CR@P.. there's no substitute for a professionally done job.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>(unless you have the equipment to do it yourself, which I don't.. plus, it'd cost more to buy the decal paper than to buy a resdy made one!)<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||11
